{
 "schemaVersion": 1,
 "id": "kukhnya-s01e14-scene-13",
 "pair": "ru-en",
 "title": "Где шеф?  (Where is the Chef?)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "diana": "Диана",
  "max": "Макс",
  "nagiyev": "Нагиев"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "The guests are asking for the chef, but Barinov has passed out. Nagiyev finds Max hiding in the kitchen and tells him to cook. Listen in Russian first.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "diana",
   "t": "Витя, просыпайтесь!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Он не проснется.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Бесполезно его будить.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Максимилиан, вот вы где.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Да, я здесь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Вы прячетесь от нас.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я ни от кого не прячусь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Приготовьте нам маленький шедевр.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Мы хотим старинную французскую кухню.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Шеф-повару нужно отдыхать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "У нас производственное совещание.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Максимилиан, я вас жду.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я сейчас к вам приду.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Again, line by line.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "diana",
   "t": "Витя, просыпайтесь!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Vitya, wake up!' 'Vitya' is a pet form of Viktor. The 'wake up' order ends in 'tes', for a group or for politeness, and the 'sya' is there because you wake yourself.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Он не проснется.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'He will not wake up.' 'Prosnyotsya' is 'will wake up', and 'ne' in front makes it 'will not'. Nagiyev says it flatly.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Бесполезно его будить.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'It is useless to wake him.' 'Useless' is built from 'without' and 'use'. To wake someone else is a different word from waking yourself.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Максимилиан, вот вы где.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Maximilian, there you are.' 'Vot vy gde' is a handy phrase for 'there you are', literally 'here you where'. Nagiyev invents a grand name for Max.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Да, я здесь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Yes, I am here.' 'Zdes' is 'here', and there is no 'am'. Max keeps it short.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Вы прячетесь от нас.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You are hiding from us.' The 'sya' on the end means 'hide yourselves', and 'from us' follows. The polite plural is used for Max.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я ни от кого не прячусь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I am not hiding from anyone.' Russian says 'from nobody not'. The 'ne' stays even though 'nobody' already has the 'no'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Приготовьте нам маленький шедевр.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Prepare a little masterpiece for us.' The polite order 'prepare!' ends in 'te'. A 'little masterpiece' is a joke, since nobody makes one on demand.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Мы хотим старинную французскую кухню.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We want classic French cuisine.' 'Old-time' describes the cuisine, and the word for cuisine is the one for 'kitchen'. Both end in 'uyu' because they're what is wanted.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Шеф-повару нужно отдыхать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'A chef needs to rest.' Russian says 'to the chef it is needed'. 'Rest' stays in its basic form.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "У нас производственное совещание.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We have a production meeting.' 'Proizvodstvennoe soveshchanie' is a long, heavy phrase for a 'production meeting'. Nagiyev is making something up to sound important.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Максимилиан, я вас жду.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Maximilian, I am waiting for you.' Literally, 'I you wait', with no 'for'. The polite 'you' is the form after 'wait'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я сейчас к вам приду.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I will come to you now.' The 'k' in front of 'you' means 'towards'. 'I will come' is one word that tells you the person arrives on foot. Now the whole scene again.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "diana",
   "t": "Витя, просыпайтесь!",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Он не проснется.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Бесполезно его будить.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Максимилиан, вот вы где.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Да, я здесь.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Вы прячетесь от нас.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я ни от кого не прячусь.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Приготовьте нам маленький шедевр.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Мы хотим старинную французскую кухню.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Шеф-повару нужно отдыхать.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "У нас производственное совещание.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Максимилиан, я вас жду.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я сейчас к вам приду.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Max walks out to the table, and he has no idea what he's about to cook. Nagiyev is polite to him throughout. See you next time.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Пока!",
   "gap": 0.3
  }
 ],
